The indexer (polyphony) began as a fork of TxPipe's Scrolls
(https://github.com/txpipe/scrolls, Apache-2.0) and has since been
substantially rewritten; portions of the original remain. It is built on
the gasket staged-pipeline framework (https://github.com/construkts/gasket-rs,
Apache-2.0). Chain access is built on TxPipe's Pallas
(https://github.com/txpipe/pallas, Apache-2.0). Plutus script evaluation
uses uplc from the Aiken project (https://github.com/aiken-lang/aiken,
Apache-2.0), via a maintained fork. The stack uses maintained forks of the
TiKV Rust client and bb8-tikv, published under the maestro-org GitHub
organisation.

The optional `full` compose profile installs, at deploy time, the Koios SQL
layer from the Cardano Community's koios-artifacts
(https://github.com/cardano-community/koios-artifacts, CC-BY-4.0) and builds
the pg_bech32 Postgres extension
(https://github.com/cardano-community/pg_bech32, WTFPL), which links against
libbech32 (https://github.com/whitslack/libbech32, WTFPL). These are fetched
or built at deploy time and are not distributed as part of this repository,
with one exception: services/mapi/migrations/dataplane contains two SQL
functions adapted from koios-artifacts (CC-BY-4.0), modified as described in
their file headers.
